**Finding (Correctness — Required):** Subtracting `getMilliseconds()` values only compares the `0–999` millisecond field of each `Date`. Intervals spanning full seconds return `0` when the sub-second digits match or negative numbers when milliseconds wrap around.

**Scope & Checks:** Reviewed the single PR line statically; no test runner was executed.

**Correction:**
```ts
const elapsed = end.getTime() - start.getTime();
```

**Regression Example:**
```ts
import assert from "node:assert/strict";

function measureElapsed(start: Date, end: Date): number {
  const elapsed = end.getTime() - start.getTime();
  return elapsed;
}

const start = new Date("2026-01-01T12:00:00.250Z");
const twoSecondsLater = new Date("2026-01-01T12:00:02.250Z");
const wrappedSecond = new Date("2026-01-01T12:00:01.050Z");

assert.equal(measureElapsed(start, twoSecondsLater), 2000);
assert.equal(measureElapsed(start, wrappedSecond), 800);
```
